If, so, Section 141 C. P. C. is directly attracted. It reads;
"The procedure provided in this Code in regard to suits shall be followed, as far as it can be made applicable, in all proceedings in any court of civil jurisdiction."
By reason of this section, the provisions of Order 1 apply to a writ proceeding as far as they can be made applicable to such a proceeding. The relevant rules applicable to the joinder of more than one plaintiff in one suit are Order 1 Rule 1 and Order 2 Rule 3.
